# Foundry VTT System Development (V13)

**Authoritative docs:** [Foundry Virtual Tabletop API v13](https://foundryvtt.com/api/)

## Production Package First
- Build with `npm run build` and copy the resulting package (`system.json`, `dist/`, `templates/`, `lang/`, `assets|icons/`, `packs/`) into `Data/systems/<id>` for testing.
- `system.json.esmodules` and `system.json.styles` must reference built files in `/systems/${game.system.id}/dist/…`; never point at `src/` or localhost URLs.
- Maintain the `compatibility` object (`minimum`, `maximum`, `verified`) so it reflects the Foundry versions validated with each release.
- Bump `system.json.version` whenever shipped assets change to bust caches and keep migrations orderly.

## Source vs. Runtime Layout
- Source lives under `/src`, `/templates`, `/lang`, `/assets` (or `/icons`), and `/packs/_source`.
- Builds emit to `/dist`; do not require a dev server for the installed package.
- The top-level entry (for example `src/index.ts`) registers hooks, sheets, settings, and Handlebars helpers. Favor `ApplicationV2` and `DocumentSheetV2` when creating UI per v13 guidance.
- See `[dynamic-paths.mdc](mdc:dynamic-paths.mdc)` and `[id-match.mdc](mdc:id-match.mdc)` for canonical path and identifier rules.

## Data, Packs, and Migrations
- Author compendium data in `/packs/_source`, compile to `.db` under `/packs` before release, and keep packs domain-focused.
- On `Hooks.once("ready")`, run version-gated migrations that read the stored system version, apply idempotent transforms, then save the new version.

## Diagnostics and QA
- Log a single startup line naming the system, version, and Foundry compatibility target.
- Keep console noise low—see `[console-clarity.mdc](mdc:console-clarity.mdc)`—so real errors surface.
- Provide scripts/tests that confirm:
  - folder name matches `system.json.id`
  - every `esmodules[]` and `styles[]` file exists under `dist/`
  - `localhost:` and `http://127.0.0.1` are absent from the shipped bundle
  - production package loads without 404s when installed manually

## Dev-Server Option (Fallback)
- Vite dev server is optional: gate it behind `if (import.meta.env.DEV)` and ensure production builds run standalone.
- Supply `dev` scripts only as a helper once the production build path is stable; do not couple runtime features to the proxy.

## Release Discipline
- Ship tagged builds that bundle only production-safe assets (see `[sr-like-sys.mdc](mdc:sr-like-sys.mdc)` and `[repo-topology.mdc](mdc:repo-topology.mdc)`).
- Honor content boundaries and clean-room rules—refer to `[content-boundaries.mdc](mdc:content-boundaries.mdc)` and `[prime-directive.mdc](mdc:prime-directive.mdc)`.